      "provenance": {
        "kind": "handwritten",
        "rationale": "The accept half of the P1-B pair. A buy bound to outcome 0 and a sell bound to outcome 1 is exactly the book on which the scalar relation matched one unit, charged a fee, and then refused every settlement. Under the coupled relation the book still clears, but only as the empty candidate: zero flow on both outcomes, zero consideration, zero fee, zero weighted direct volume, and no participating owner. The digest and score were read off the implementation's own recomputation at these coordinates; they are the value the relation defines as canonical, and step 0 pins them so no later step can rely on an unpinned derivation.",
        "source": "crates/clutch-batch/src/relation_v1_tests.rs (relation_v1_cross_outcome_pair_cannot_produce_matched_volume)"
      },
      "status": "proposed",
      "surface": "clutch-batch",
      "title": "P1-B: a cross-outcome pair clears only as the empty candidate, with no fee-eligible volume"
    },
