      "provenance": {
        "kind": "handwritten",
        "rationale": "The refuse half of the P1-B pair, and the whole point of the coupled relation. Per-outcome conservation with one global virtual split/merge pair requires the same net imbalance c on every active outcome; a fill of 1 on outcome 0's buy and 1 on outcome 1's sell forces c = -1 on outcome 0 and c = +1 on outcome 1 simultaneously, so the system has no solution. Both entry points are exercised because the module documents a deliberate V4-before-V3 precedence: the diagnostic 5026 must be reported rather than the generic 5009, and step 0 shows the full verifier reaches the same conclusion before its V9 aggregate binding.",
        "source": "crates/clutch-batch/src/relation_v1_tests.rs (relation_v1_cross_outcome_pair_cannot_produce_matched_volume)"
      },
